---
title: "Krewire Release — Official Release Launch & Community Hub"
description: "The official launchpad, contributor portal, and sponsorship hub for the Krewire open-source ecosystem."
layout: Landing
---

<div class="contributors-portal">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-i18n="hero.eyebrow">◈ OFFICIAL RELEASE LAUNCH · KREWIRE ECOSYSTEM</div>
        <h1 data-i18n-html="hero.title_html">Krewire v0.1.0 is Here.<br>Build the Future of Go.</h1>
        <p class="lead" data-i18n="hero.lead">Welcome to the official launchpad and community hub for Krewire. A unified, modular Go ecosystem powering 8 workloads behind one config and one CLI — engineered in Indonesia for engineers and autonomous AI agents worldwide.</p>
        <div class="ctas flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <Button Variant="primary" Size="lg" Href="#releases" DataI18n="hero.cta_release">Explore v0.1.0 Launch →</Button>
          <Button Variant="outline" Size="lg" Href="#get-started" DataI18n="hero.cta_start">Become a Contributor</Button>
          <Button Variant="outline" Size="lg" Href="#sponsorship" DataI18n="hero.cta_sponsor">Sponsor Krewire</Button>
        </div>
        <div class="meta" data-i18n="hero.meta">Go 1.27.1+ · Single Monorepo · 8 Unified Workloads · Strict Quality Gates</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art">
        <CodeWindow />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TRUST BAR -->
  <section class="trust">
    <div class="trust-inner">
      <span class="trust-label" data-i18n="trust.label">Ecosystem Launch Matrix</span>
      <div class="trust-items">
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.repos_html"><b>5</b> Official Repositories</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.workloads_html"><b>8</b> Unified Workloads</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.native_html"><b>100%</b> Native Go</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n-html="trust.version_html"><b>v0.1.0</b> Stable Baseline</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span data-i18n="trust.cost">Near-Zero Cloud Cost</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RELEASE LAUNCH SECTION -->
  <section class="releases" id="releases" style="padding: 64px 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
    <div class="section-inner" style="max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="section-head text-center" style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
        <div class="sub-badge" style="display: inline-block; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 9999px; background: rgba(57, 211, 83, 0.1); color: var(--primary); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Ecosystem Release</div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 32px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 12px;">Krewire Ecosystem v0.1.0 Launch</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--muted); max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; font-size: 16px;">The complete foundational release of the Krewire modular Go libraries, devtool CLI, and developer workflow.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="release-grid" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 40px;">
        <div class="release-card" style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--bg-card, rgba(255,255,255,0.03)); border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <div style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 12px;">📦</div>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Single Monorepo</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">Consolidated under <code>github.com/krewire/krewire</code> — seamless module resolution, atomic versioning, and zero dependency fragmentation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="release-card" style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--bg-card, rgba(255,255,255,0.03)); border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <div style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 12px;">⚡</div>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Unified 'kiw' Devtool</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">One single binary managing the entire software lifecycle: <code>kiw init</code>, <code>kiw new</code>, <code>kiw dev</code>, <code>kiw build</code>, and <code>kiw deploy</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="release-card" style="padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--bg-card, rgba(255,255,255,0.03)); border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <div style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 12px;">⚙️</div>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">One Config: krewire.yaml</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">Strictly typed, declarative project manifests eliminating arbitrary configuration drift across all 8 supported workloads.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="quickstart-box" style="padding: 32px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--bg-dark, #0B1F3B); border: 1px solid var(--border); color: #fff; text-align: center;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Quick Start in Seconds</h3>
        <p style="color: #9ab0ce; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 20px;">Initialize a project minimal setup or scaffold a complete fullstack application:</p>
        <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); padding: 14px 20px; border-radius: 8px; font-family: monospace; font-size: 14px; color: #39D353; display: inline-block; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; text-align: left;">
          kiw new my-app && cd my-app && kiw dev
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
          <a href="https://krewire.com" target="_blank" style="color: #39D353; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; text-decoration: underline;">Read Full Documentation on krewire.com →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PILLARS / PHILOSOPHY -->
  <section class="pillars" id="philosophy">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="pillars.badge">Philosophy</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pillars.title">Engineered for Autonomy, Built for Longevity</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pillars.subtitle">Krewire is not just another web framework. It is an open architectural collective solving software fragmentation, ballooning cloud costs, and developer fatigue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-grid">
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p1_title">Autonomous by Design</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p1_desc">Built from ground up to support self-healing, self-building pipelines, and native orchestration by autonomous AI agents (Boost).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">📐</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p2_title">Spec-Driven Development (SDD)</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p2_desc">Zero hand-waving. Every architectural boundary begins with formal specifications (<code>KWF-*</code>) and clear contract interfaces before implementation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">🌱</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p3_title">Near-Zero Cloud Cost</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p3_desc">Radical resource efficiency. Go standard-library minimalism designed to operate smoothly on $5 VPS nodes up to hyperscale infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">🤝</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="pillars.p4_title">Human-AI Synergy</h3>
          <p data-i18n="pillars.p4_desc">Specialized AI agents (Boost) act as first-class team members — auditing security, catching regressions, and helping contributors iterate faster.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTRIBUTOR BENEFITS & LIFETIME ACCESS -->
  <section class="benefits" id="benefits">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="benefits.badge">Contributor Privilege</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="benefits.title">Lifetime Access to Krewire's Paid Ecosystem</h2>
        <p data-i18n="benefits.subtitle">Genuine appreciation for true builders. By joining and actively contributing to the Krewire open source collective, you earn lifetime access to our upcoming commercial sub-products and premium ecosystem tools.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-grid">
        <div class="benefit-card highlight">
          <div class="benefit-badge" data-i18n="benefits.b1_badge">Core Privilege</div>
          <div class="benefit-icon">★</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="benefits.b1_title">Commercial Sub-Products Lifetime Access</h3>
          <p data-i18n="benefits.b1_desc">Receive free lifetime licenses for upcoming commercial Krewire products — including managed cloud orchestration tools, enterprise modules, and premium services.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b1_i1">Free lifetime access to all paid Krewire commercial sub-products</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b1_i2">Priority early-access releases and exclusive roadmap previews</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b1_i3">Direct private collaboration channels with core maintainers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-card condition">
          <div class="benefit-badge req" data-i18n="benefits.b2_badge">Strict Requirement</div>
          <div class="benefit-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="benefits.b2_title">Active Contributions Required</h3>
          <p data-i18n="benefits.b2_desc">This privilege is a two-way commitment. Your access remains active as long as you regularly contribute and help nurture the ecosystem's growth.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b2_i1">Submit PRs for new features, bugfixes, or kernel optimizations</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b2_i2">Review open PRs and stress-test high-concurrency scenarios</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b2_i3">Author KWF architecture specifications or comprehensive docs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-card notice">
          <div class="benefit-badge warn" data-i18n="benefits.b3_badge">Revocation Policy</div>
          <div class="benefit-icon">⚠</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="benefits.b3_title">Revocable if Inactive or Dormant</h3>
          <p data-i18n="benefits.b3_desc">To protect community fairness and true meritocracy, commercial access licenses may be revoked at any time if a contributor becomes inactive or dormant over an extended period.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b3_i1">Contributor activity and commits are periodically audited</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b3_i2">Prolonged inactivity or dormancy leads to license deactivation</li>
            <li data-i18n="benefits.b3_i3">Access privileges can be promptly reinstated upon resumed contribution</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-policy-banner">
        <div class="policy-marker">◈</div>
        <div class="policy-text">
          <strong data-i18n="benefits.policy_title">Krewire Meritocracy Policy:</strong>
          <span data-i18n="benefits.policy_text">We believe those who lay the foundation should share in its fruits. Commercial access is free for all active contributors, provided ongoing dedication to the collective is consistently maintained.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- UNIFIED CODEBASE MATRIX & CONTRIBUTOR NAVIGATOR -->
